---
// The privacy policy. One page, in UK English, for both languages: the
// stores link to this address. The wording is the policy as published on
// 15 October 2026, with read-aloud and the microphone added on 10 November
// 2026 for 1.4.0 (src/speech/ in the app's repository, and its own Privacy &
// data screen, app/privacy.tsx), and Redeem a code and Settings for 1.4.1
// (src/purchases/purchaseState.ts, src/config/redeem.ts); change the date whenever the text changes.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { UK, path, breadcrumbs } from '../lib/site.js';

const trail = [
  { name: 'Home', path: path(UK, 'home') },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy/' },
];
---
<Base
  locale={UK}
  kind="privacy"
  paired={false}
  pathname="/privacy/"
  appBar={false}
  title="Privacy Policy - Dad Hair Hero"
  description="Dad Hair Hero collects no personal data. No accounts, no analytics, no ad tracking. What the app stores stays on your device and in your own backup."
  trail={trail}
  jsonld={[breadcrumbs(trail)]}
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 10 November 2026</p>

  <p>Dad Hair Hero does not collect, transmit or store your personal data on any server. We have no accounts, no analytics, no ad networks or ad tracking, and no crash reporting.</p>

  <p>What the app stores. Everything you enter — your child's name, hair type and age band, your progress, and any photos and notes you add to the style diary — is saved on your device. None of it is sent to Dad Hair Hero or to anyone else. We cannot see it.</p>

  <p>Backups. If your device backs itself up (iCloud, or Android backup), what the app stores is part of that backup, photos and notes included, like any other app. That backup is yours, in your own Apple or Google account. It is never sent to Dad Hair Hero.</p>

  <p>Photos. The app asks for camera and photo library access only when you choose to add a photo to the diary. Photos are saved in the app's own storage on your device. If you share a photo using your phone's share options, it goes wherever you send it — never to us.</p>
  <p>Read aloud. Steps are read aloud by your phone's own voice. Dad Hair Hero doesn't record or send anything.</p>

  <p>Microphone and speech recognition. While you follow a style's steps, you can say "next", "back" or "repeat" instead of tapping. This is off unless you turn it on, and the app asks for the microphone (and, on iPhone, speech recognition) the first time you do; it is never requested at launch. Then your phone's own speech recognition listens, on the phone, only while a style is open, for next, back and repeat. Dad Hair Hero doesn't record, keep or send what it hears: no audio and no transcript is stored, logged or counted, and the only thing the app saves is whether you turned it on. It stops listening when the app goes into the background or the screen locks. The app offers it only on phones that can recognise speech on the phone itself, and asks for that every time, so what you say is never sent to a speech service to be recognised.</p>

  <p>Sharing a page. The "Send this to him" button on a style page uses your phone's own share sheet, or copies the link for you, and nothing is sent to Dad Hair Hero. The link it shares names the page and a campaign, so the app stores can count installs from shared pages; it carries nothing about you.</p>

  <p>Links to shops. The Kit section contains affiliate links to product pages. Tapping one opens your normal browser, and we may earn a small commission on purchases. Once you leave the app, the site you land on has its own privacy policy, which we don't control.</p>

  <p>In-app purchases. Beyond the Ponytail is an optional one-time purchase. If you buy it, the App Store or Google Play takes the payment through your store account. Dad Hair Hero never receives your payment or card details. The app only asks the store for the price of the pack and whether you have bought it. Nothing is sent to us.</p>

  <p>Redeeming a code. Settings in the app has "Redeem a code". It opens the store's own place to enter a code: Apple's offer-code sheet on an iPhone, or Google Play's redeem page on Android. You type the code into the App Store or Google Play, not into Dad Hair Hero, and the app never sees it. A code the store accepts counts as a purchase of the pack, and the app learns only what it learns from a purchase: whether you own the pack.</p>

  <p>Deleting your data. The app's Privacy &amp; data screen, reached from Settings (the gear on the Us tab), has a "Delete everything" option. It removes all stored data and every diary and Wall of Fame photo from your device. The app will restart as if it has never been opened. This cannot be undone.</p>

  <p>Three things are kept. Your spelling choice. The record of which styles are yours, so deleting never costs you a style you already had. And whether Today has already suggested Beyond the Ponytail, so it is never suggested twice. A purchase stays with your App Store or Google Play account.</p>

  <p>Uninstalling the app also removes what it stores from your device.</p>

  <p>Images. The pictures of hairstyles in the app and on this website are illustrations of a mannequin head. None of them is a photograph of a child. The one real photograph on this website is on the About page, of Martin and his daughter, and she is a silhouette in it.</p>

  <p>Children. This app is designed for adults. It is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect data from anyone.</p>

  <p>Contact. hello@dadhairhero.com</p>
</Base>
